# Naming rationale is load-bearing docs

`README.md` must open with the naming rationale: title, tagline, then a
**`## Why "repave"?`** section — before the pitch, the pipeline diagram, the version
callout, or anything else. `docs/concepts.md` carries the longer form as its first
section (**`## Why "repave"`**).

## Rules

- **Never drop or relocate it.** Docs cleanups, README restructures, and length trims keep
 this section first. It has been lost once already and was not recoverable from git history.
- **Do not bury it** under "Why teams use repave" (that section is about buyer value; this
 one is about the name and the thesis behind it).
- **Edit for wording, not for meaning.** The thesis is: platform teams pave roads; roads
 crack as standards move; repave re-renders artifacts from a versioned blueprint instead of
 patching each repo in place — pave once, repave when the standard moves.
- Keep it to a short paragraph or two in the README; `docs/concepts.md` may go deeper and
 should tie the other concepts (blueprints, gates, `repave.yaml`, operator) back to it.

## Why this rule exists

The name is the product thesis, not branding. A reader who does not get "repave" does not
get why generation is deterministic, why gates cannot be bypassed, or why the operator
opens upgrade PRs.
